Ah. Odds are very much against your never angering your god by praying
(the wait time between prays has no upper limit). Once your god is pissed
off, only sacrificing will make things all hotsy-totsy and chummy between
you and Him. Of course, if you don't find an appropriate altar.. But wait!
you can can convert altars to the right alignment, can't you? Umm.. as it turns
out, angry gods tend to be suspicious and are liable to regard such attempts 
at altar conversion as proof of a turn-coat nature. So, my advice is, 
find an altar, if it isn't the right one, convert it and _then_ pray all 
you want.

